  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Nor'easter filling as its center pushes inland \nmeanders across Southern New Jersey late today and tonight.\n\nThe center of the nor-easter is located between KACY and KMIV\nthis afternoon and the low is expected to push just a bot more\nto the southwest early tonight before becoming nearly \nstationary over Southern NJ or Delaware Bay later tonight. The \ncenter of the low will drift slowly offshore again Monday and \ntrack south of and parallel with the southern shore of Long \nIsland. \n\nOne distinct vort lobe will bring several hours more of mainly \nlight rain across the region to the west of a KHGR to KIPT and\nKELM line late this afternoon through early tonight. \n\nA second area of rain associated with mid level FGEN forcing\njust NW of the low center will move back into the Western\nPoconos and Susq Valley this evening and fall off and on as\nlight rain or drizzle overnight with another 0.10 to 0.25 of an\ninch expected.\n\nNortherly wind gusts in the mid to upper 20 kt range will\npersist across the Susq Valley into the early evening hours\nbefore slipping back into the teens.\n\nConditions will improve (with respect to less rain) tonight and\nMonday morning. By noon Monday, there should only be isolated \n--SHRA over the NE and the wind will not be notable. Temps rise \nslightly from Sun, but will still be cooler than normal. \n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Tranquil conditions expected for the first half \nof next week with a slight warming trend emerging across the \nregion.\n\nDry conditions will continue into Thursday as the front\nanticipated to be arriving late Wed/night will be delayed for a\nday or so. It will pick up some moisture from the remnants of\nPolo. But, that precip probably stays to our W until Thursday. All\nmodel guidance trends towards a warming trend in this \ntimeframe, with above-average temperatures prevailing area wide\nfor the balance of the week. Someone may hit 80F before Friday.\nDetails on timing and intensity of rainfall are not easy to pin\ndown at this range and with the upcoming pattern. So, we'll just\nmake a gradual increase in PoPs Fri-Sat-Sun.",
